---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pressure Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Pressure Easy - Blood Pressure Tracker iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/pressure-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Pressure Easy?</p>
          <p>Check the FAQ below or send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Pressure%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What do the blood pressure categories mean?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Pressure Easy uses the American Heart Association (AHA) guidelines to classify your readings:</p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                <li><strong class="text-green-600 dark:text-green-400">Normal:</strong> Less than 120/80 mmHg</li>
                <li><strong class="text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-400">Elevated:</strong> 120-129 / less than 80 mmHg</li>
                <li><strong class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400">High Stage 1:</strong> 130-139 / 80-89 mmHg</li>
                <li><strong class="text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">High Stage 2:</strong> 140+ / 90+ mmHg</li>
                <li><strong class="text-red-800 dark:text-red-300">Crisis:</strong> 180+ / 120+ mmHg — seek medical attention</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">When should I measure my blood pressure?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">For the most accurate readings:</p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-[var(--text-secondary)] list-disc list-inside">
                <li>Measure at the same times each day (morning and evening)</li>
                <li>Rest for 5 minutes before measuring</li>
                <li>Sit with your back supported and feet flat on the floor</li>
                <li>Don't smoke, drink caffeine, or exercise 30 minutes before</li>
                <li>Take 2-3 readings, 1 minute apart, and record the average</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Pressure Easy sync with Apple Health?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes! HealthKit integration is optional. You can choose to read existing blood pressure data from Apple Health and/or write new readings to it. Your data stays on your device — we never see it.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I share my readings with my doctor?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Go to the Trends tab and tap the export button. Pressure Easy generates a professional PDF report with all your readings and statistics. You can then email it, AirDrop it, or print it for your appointment.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I log readings on my Apple Watch?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes! The Apple Watch app provides a quick, step-by-step flow to log systolic, diastolic, and pulse readings. It syncs automatically with your iPhone.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is Pressure Easy a medical device?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">No. Pressure Easy is a tracking tool to help you log and visualize your blood pressure readings. It does not measure blood pressure — you need a blood pressure monitor for that. Always consult your healthcare provider for medical advice.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="border-b border-[var(--border-color)] pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where is my data stored?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">All your data is stored locally on your device. There's no cloud sync, no accounts, and no servers involved. Your blood pressure readings are private and stay private.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="pb-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I change the color theme?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Go to Settings and choose from 8 beautiful color themes. Each theme also includes a matching app icon that you can apply.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
